 "signature": null,
 "observations": [
  "col_left L1, L37: «al-Biṭrūǵī» and «al-Ǵayhānī» are printed with ǵ and Ǵ, Nallino's sign for jīm; their final ī have bars (2.5-2.6 by 1.0 points), measured with macron_audit.py.",
  "col_left L10: the foot of the small-capital L of «{sc:xlii}» is printed apart from its stem and slanting (1.8 by 2.0 points, on the baseline), like a comma; it is part of the L, not a comma.",
  "col_left L13: «‘Immānū’ēl» begins with the sign of ‘ayn (a turned comma) and has the sign of hamza (an apostrophe) between ū and ē; in «Ya‘ăqōb» the second a has a breve and the ō is the sort with its macron joined to the top of the o (as in Yōsēph, p. 380).",
  "col_left L15: the ṣ of «*aṣ-ṣayyāḥ*» (twice) and its ḥ have their dots below.",
  "col_left L20: the comma after «301» is printed short, like a point (1.7 by 2.0 points, its narrowed foot 0.5 point below the baseline), as on pp. 366-367, 370 and 374-375.",
  "col_left L23: the Arabic «بزرك» is printed with the final kāf in its isolated form: a slanting upper stroke and the small hamza-like mark inside the bowl, as the kāf of «الفلك» in the glossary (p. 323); the type prints gāf as kāf with three dots (ڭ, glossary p. 335), and the name, Persian Bozorg, is transcribed as printed.",
  "col_left L32: a speck (0.7 by 0.6 point) on the baseline before «183» is not transcribed.",
  "col_left L35: the point after the first «n» is printed small (1.0 by 1.0 point).",
  "col_left L37: the middle 3 of «323» is printed broken.",
  "col_left L40, L41: the dots under the t of «*al-awsaṭ*» and of «*aṭ-ṭālib*» (twice) are printed; the ā of «*ṭālib*» has its macron.",
  "col_right L1: the o of «(Boulliau)» is printed broken, open on the right.",
  "col_right L9, L10: a blank line separates the names in B from those in C.",
  "col_right L10, L11, L12: the guillemets around «paxillus Terrae» and «paxillus medii Caeli» are printed as small solid wedges, as on pp. 366, 370, 374 and 377.",
  "col_right L11: «μεσουράνημα» is Greek, with the acute on the second α.",
  "col_right L13: the hyphen of «*al-ḥisāb*» is printed as a point at mid height; the ṣ and the ḥ of «*aṣḥāb*» and the ḥ of «*ḥisāb*» have their dots below.",
  "col_right L14: a blot of ink at the foot of the first I of «II» is not transcribed.",
  "col_right L20: a short stroke at mid height joined to the left of the parenthesis after «*172*» is not transcribed.",
  "col_right L26: the middle 5 of «155» is printed broken, its top open like E.",
  "col_right L31: «(?)» is printed with a question mark of a narrower design than that of the text.",
  "col_right L35: a speck (0.6 by 0.6 point) above the last comma of the line is not transcribed; the comma is not a semicolon.",
  "col_right L41: the first d of «*codd.*» is printed broken.",
  "col_right L45: the entry Caussin goes on on p. 382."
 ],
